DTSTAMP:20260502T031955Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260502T093000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260502T123000
SUMMARY:Updated: The Biltmore Farm Trail Is Fairly Flat and a 6 Mile Round
  Trip—Join Us!
DESCRIPTION:Haywood County Walking Meetup Group\n**Update: The Farm Trail 
 and the Arbor Trace Trail are currently closed (as of March 8). If still c
 losed on May 2\, we will walk the Lagoon Trail instead. The start point is
  the same\, but the distance is shorter.**\n\nIn front of the Antler Hill 
 Barn\, by the Playground\, there is a picnic shelter known as the Antler H
 ill Pavillion. We will meet there at 9:30 a.m.\n\nWe will walk the seldom-
 done Farm Trail along the French Broad River edge of the estate property\,
  mostly out and back. Biltmore says it is a 6-mile (10 KM) round trip.\n\n
 Dress for the weather. Bring a protein snack and water. Walking sticks onl
 y if you want them since the walk will be mostly level. Tennis shoes shoul
 d be okay\, unless it has rained a lot recently\, in which case light hiki
 ng boots would be better. Dogs are welcome. Trail strollers should work ok
 .\n\nYou will need a grounds pass\, so arrive no later than 9 a.m. to purc
 hase it and let me know so we will wait to start the walk until you have j
 oined us. We actually recommend the purchase of an annual pass\, as we wil
 l be walking on the estate grounds several times in the coming year.
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/haywood-county-walking-meetup-group/e
 vents/313050558/
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CREATED:20260125T170241Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260125T170241Z
CLASS:PUBLIC
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Ncarboretum": "https://www.ncarboretum.org/event/bonsai-in-a-day-learn-create-take-home/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:ncarboretum
X-SOURCE:NC Arboretum
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260502T093000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260502T163000
DTSTAMP:20260501T231958
CREATED:20260319T184924Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260427T194443Z
UID:10017000-1777714200-1777739400@www.ncarboretum.org
SUMMARY:Bonsai in a Day: Learn\, Create\, Take Home (full\, more sessions to come!)
DESCRIPTION:Bonsai in a Day: Learn\, Create\, Take Home\nwith Rebecca Ayres \nSaturday\, May 2  |  9:30am – 4:30pm \nREGISTER HERE \nAlthough it has its roots in ancient Asian traditions\, the living art of bonsai now enjoys enthusiasts throughout much of the world. This class will provide the basic concepts and skills for novices to begin growing and shaping their own miniature trees. The first half of the class will cover the fundamental horticultural and aesthetic principles of bonsai. It will include such topics as tree selection\, watering\, pest control\, pruning\, wiring\, and styling. In the second half of the class\, each participant will receive a pot\, scissors\, wire\, and planting medium. With guidance from the instructor\, the students will create their own bonsai to take home. Materials included in registration. \nRebecca Ayres is a ceramic artist and gardener. A longtime Arboretum volunteer\, she is the assistant to the bonsai curator and helps with overseeing the exhibition garden\, the collection and the Carolina Bonsai Expo. She is a member of the Blue Ridge Bonsai Society\, where she has taught workshops and classes\, and is a graduate of the Arboretum’s Blue Ridge Naturalist program. \n\nMembers: Remember to enter your promo code upon checkout to receive your 10% member discount! Email adulteducation@ncarboretum.org with questions.\nSee a full listing of Adult Education Programs at the North Carolina Arboretum here! Questions? Check our FAQs.\nWe are committed to fostering a diverse\, supportive learning community. If the cost of a class is a barrier for you\, please complete this scholarship form and we will see what kind of assistance we can provide.\nFollow us on Facebook & Instagram!\nJoin our Adult Education Student Hub on Discord!\nInterested in supporting the NC Arboretum more directly? Donate to the ONE Fund here.\n\nSee all of our classes open for registration here!
URL:https://www.ncarboretum.org/event/bonsai-in-a-day-learn-create-take-home/
CATEGORIES:Adult Education
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://www.ncarboretum.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/03/Bonsai.jpg
END:VEVENT
