X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Meetup Asheville Mountains To Sea Trail Hiking Club": "https://www.meetup.com/asheville-mountains-to-sea-trail-hiking-club/events/314103961/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:meetup_asheville_mountains_to_sea_trail_hiking_club
X-SOURCE:Asheville Mountains-to-Sea Trail Hiking Club
UID:event_314103961@meetup.com
SEQUENCE:1
DTSTAMP:20260502T031948Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260504T090000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260504T110000
SUMMARY:Craven Gap
DESCRIPTION:Asheville Mountains-to-Sea Trail Hiking Club 2.0\nThis is a fa
 irly undulating hike. It's narrow at first with some rocky steps and then 
 narrow and rooty for most of the way until halfway when there's a short cl
 imb to the 2.5 mile mark. We go about 2.7 to 2.9 mph.\n\nWell behaved dogs
  on leashes are welcome to attend.\n\nWhen you arrive\, park at the gravel
  lot on the other side of the road\, closest to Town Mountain. You'll see 
 some people gathering by their cars.\n\nMountains-to-Sea-Trail hikes are d
 esigned for fitness and community among people who are already reasonably 
 fit. It's not an endurance hike by any means\, but it is designed so we ca
 n get our hearts beating a bit while still being able to have a conversati
 on and meet new people.\nWhen you arrive\, we'll circle up and introduce o
 urselves briefly. There will be a person who is a sweep. This person is th
 e person who walks last and makes sure no one gets lost.\n\nWe leave the p
 arking spot at 9:10. If someone needs a nature break\, we wait fo you\, bu
 t it's not a hike where we stop and take photos or frequent breaks. We bas
 ically keep hiking until the 1/2 way mark\, then turn around after a short
  (approximately 5 minute) break. Then we keep that same pace on the way ba
 ck. If we get on a trail right at 9:10\, we are normally finished around 1
 0:50.\n\nThese are out and back hikes\, meaning that we hike in and turn a
 round half way to return back.
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/asheville-mountains-to-sea-trail-hiki
 ng-club/events/314103961/
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CREATED:20260403T110246Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260403T110246Z
CLASS:PUBLIC
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Meetup Ashevillehikinggroup": "https://www.meetup.com/ashevillehikinggroup/events/314569724/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:meetup_ashevillehikinggroup
X-SOURCE:Asheville Hiking Group
UID:event_314569724@meetup.com
SEQUENCE:1
DTSTAMP:20260502T031946Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260504T091500
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260504T140000
SUMMARY:Explorer Loop Trailhead to MST over to Green Top and DOWN - 7.5 Mi
 les 1800 Ft
DESCRIPTION:The Asheville Hiking Group\n**Details**\n\n* 7.5 Miles\, 1700 
 Ft elevation gain with a STEEP downhill.\n* Carpool meeting time is 9:15 a
 t the Asheville Outlets parking lot behind the Waffle House.\n* Sign up st
 arts Friday at 5pm\n\nThis starts as a good and steady uphill climb from t
 he Bent Creek Explorer Loop trailhead and going up to the MST by Chestnut 
 Cove. We will head up the MST beyond Bent Creek Gap Rd and back into Bent 
 Creek on the Three Humps trail before descending one of Bent Creek's steep
 est trails. It is one mile long and 1000 ft of elevation drop and don't th
 ink it will be easy! Expect to hug some trees and be amazed that people go
  down this on a mountain bike. We will do a moderate pace of about 2.7 mph
  but stop for breaks as needed.\n\nIt looks like the cooler weather is ret
 urning next week so pull back out those warm clothes.. Hopefully the wildf
 lowers will still be in bloom.\n\n**CARPOOL**\nWe will meet at the Ashevil
 le Outlets behind the Waffle House at 9:15. Please be there a little early
  so we can leave at 9:15 for the trailhead. Parking is limited at the Expl
 orer Loop trailhead so please try to carpool.\n\n**WEATHER**\nI'll watch t
 he weather and post a cancellation message by 7:30 AM if the forecast is >
 50% chance of precipitation.\n\n**QUESTIONS?**\nYou can message me through
  MeetUp until 9:00 AM the day of. Cell reception may be sketchy\, but you 
 can try to text or call me up to the start of the hike: (508) 965-2333.\n\
 n**LEGALESE**\nThis Asheville Hiking Group event involves hiking and\, pos
 sibly\, transportation to and from the meetup site. Participants are respo
 nsible for their own safety and affirm that they have the appropriate skil
 ls\, physical conditioning\, equipment\, and supplies. Hiking may involve 
 risks to oneself and property. Neither your hike organizer nor Asheville H
 iking Group can assure your safety nor eliminate all risks. Participants a
 ssume full responsibility for any injuries\, damages\, or losses.
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/ashevillehikinggroup/events/314569724
 /
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CREATED:20260501T001540Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260501T001540Z
CLASS:PUBLIC
END:VEVENT
