X-SOURCE-ID:meetup_ashevillehikinggroup
X-SOURCE:Asheville Hiking Group
UID:event_314543268@meetup.com
SEQUENCE:1
DTSTAMP:20260502T031946Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260506T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260506T210000
SUMMARY:Wednesday night Bent Creek
DESCRIPTION:The Asheville Hiking Group\n**Details**\nHard Times Trailhead 
 near Lake Powhatan Rec Area\nRSVP's don't open until 6PM Sunday night.\nWe
 ather: will know more by Tuesday and will let everyone know the details th
 en.\nI did this hike series for many years before 2022\, but I did it as a
  high-speed hike\, and I am now doing it as a moderate speed hike. This is
  a numbers limited event and I expect people who sign-up to show up. Late 
 cancellations\, and those that don't show up are bumping other interested 
 hikers\, and they will not be allowed on future hikes.\nIf all goes well\,
  I will try to post a hike most weeks\, and for days Tue or Wed\, distance
 \, and start location\, like switching between Hard Times trail-head and B
 ent Creek River Park\, may change.\nThe current route is about 5.5 miles.\
 nPlease folks\, this is intended as a moderate paced hike\, and we'd like 
 all attendees to keep up with the hike leader(s). This hike is intended as
  a workout hike for people to get in condition to do weekend hikes.\nModer
 ate paced means 22-24 min miles\, or 2 ½ mph.\nAs such\, we do not take b
 reaks\, take in views\, or snap photos along the way. Please make sure you
 're able to keep up with the group. This hike has always served as a good 
 chance to get exercise during the week\, meet new people\, and create inte
 rest for weekend enjoyment hikes. It's a great introduction to the AHG fam
 ily.\nNo need to RSVP "No" or "not attending" unless changing from a "Yes.
 "\nPlease read the full description before RSVPing\, and only sign up if y
 ou are sure you can go. Thanks in advance for keeping your RSVP up-to-date
  and not being a last-minute cancellation or no-show. This is an ongoing i
 ssue with Meetups and often keeps people on waitlists from being able to a
 ttend our hikes.\nHard Times Trailhead near Lake Powhatan Rec Area\nFollow
  signs off of Brevard Rd (Rt 191) to Lake Powhatan Rec Area. The road is B
 ent Creek Ranch Rd. to Wesley Branch Rd. Follow signs to Lake Powhatan unt
 il you come to Hard Times Trailhead on your left\, 2.5 miles. It is very c
 learly marked. Parking is very limited at the trailhead but there’s a pa
 ved pull-off just before the Hard Times trailhead and more parking just be
 yond at the Ledford Branch trailhead. We will access Bent Creek forest by 
 way of Hard Times Trail and do some combination of loop and out and back.\
 nArrive at the trailhead BY 6:00. Because it is a weeknight hike\, we are 
 unable to wait for latecomers\, fighting daylight.\n\\*\\*\\*If you are ru
 nning behind\, please post a comment on this Meetup page by 5:45 pm. There
  is no cell service at the parking lot\, so if we don't have any advance n
 otice of you running late by 5:45\, we can't get any notifications at the 
 trailhead and we will not wait for you.\nWe start the hike at 6:00\, rarel
 y do we get much later than that.\n• Wear closed-toed footwear appropria
 te for hiking. The trail will consist of dirt\, rocks\, roots\, mud and mu
 lch.\n• Bring plenty of water.\n• Bring rain gear if a chance of rain 
 is in the forecast.\nHeadlamps suggested\n• Dogs on leashes the whole ti
 me are welcome. This is an active mountain bike area and it can get messy 
 with dogs running loose among hikers and mountain bikers.\nPlease make sur
 e to keep your RSVP up-to-date. You don't want to be "that person" who can
 cels last minute or no-shows and keeps someone from joining in if there's 
 a waitlist. Thanks for your consideration - it is appreciated!\nFeel free 
 to post questions not covered in this description in the comments section.
 \nThanks - we'll see you on the trail!\nDisclaimer and Release of Liabilit
 y:\nThis activity involves hiking on city streets that may have traffic an
 d/or natural trails with roots\, rocks\, and steep sections. Participants 
 are responsible for their safety on streets and trails. The organizer of t
 his trip is a volunteer and not a professional guide. The function of the 
 organizer is only to organize this trip. If you sign up or participate in 
 this event you acknowledge that you freely and voluntarily agree to assume
  all risks of injuries\, illnesses\, and damages arising from\, as a resul
 t of\, and associated with this event. In addition\, you acknowledge that 
 you agree to the Meetup terms: [https://www.meetup.com/terms](https://www.
 meetup.com/terms)
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/ashevillehikinggroup/events/314543268
 /
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CREATED:20260429T145242Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260429T145242Z
CLASS:PUBLIC
END:VEVENT
