BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Ncarboretum": "https://www.ncarboretum.org/event/bonsai-exhibit-talk-and-tour-with-arthur-joura-2/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:ncarboretum
X-SOURCE:NC Arboretum
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260512T173000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260512T190000
DTSTAMP:20260501T231958
CREATED:20260330T155501Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260501T165016Z
UID:10017016-1778607000-1778612400@www.ncarboretum.org
SUMMARY:Bonsai Exhibit Talk and Tour with Arthur Joura
DESCRIPTION:Bonsai Exhibit Talk and Tour with Arthur Joura\nTuesday\, May 12  |  5:30 – 7pm \nREGISTER HERE \nJoin Bonsai Curator Arthur Joura on this entertaining and informative after-hours tour of the garden at its peak in spring\, a fitting showcase for the specimens and the miniature landscapes. As Joura says\, “The two things are one: The garden is designed to elevate the experience of bonsai\, and the bonsai never look better than when they’re on display in the garden.” \nThis program will take place outside and will follow easy trails and paved walkways. Dress for the weather and prepare to be outside for the entire program time. \nArthur Joura has been the bonsai curator at the Arboretum since 1992 and oversaw the design and development of the Arboretum’s Bonsai Exhibition Garden. Joura augmented early training in fine art and studied bonsai with some of the leading bonsai authorities in the United States and in Japan. His greatest teachers are trees\, however. His love of hiking and photographing trees in nature has shaped the Arboretum’s collection and firmly rooted it in a regional identify — one that elevates naturalism in art and the use of traditional bonsai species alongside species native to the Southern Appalachian mountains — creating in the process one of the most acclaimed public collections of bonsai in the country.. \n\nMembers: Remember to enter your promo code upon checkout to receive your 10% member discount! Email adulteducation@ncarboretum.org with questions.\nSee a full listing of Adult Education Programs at the North Carolina Arboretum here! Questions? Check our FAQs.\nWe are committed to fostering a diverse\, supportive learning community. If the cost of a class is a barrier for you\, please complete this scholarship form and we will see what kind of assistance we can provide.\nFollow us on Facebook & Instagram!\nJoin our Adult Education Student Hub on Discord!\nInterested in supporting the NC Arboretum more directly? Donate to the ONE Fund here.\n\nSee all of our classes open for registration here!
URL:https://www.ncarboretum.org/event/bonsai-exhibit-talk-and-tour-with-arthur-joura-2/
CATEGORIES:Adult Education
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://www.ncarboretum.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/03/Bonsai.jpg
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Meetup Shutupandwriteasheville": "https://www.meetup.com/shutupandwriteasheville/events/314426235/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:meetup_shutupandwriteasheville
X-SOURCE:Shut Up & Write Western NC
UID:event_314426235@meetup.com
SEQUENCE:1
DTSTAMP:20260502T032001Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260512T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260512T193000
SUMMARY:Shut Up & Write!® - Downtown
DESCRIPTION:Shut Up & Write!® Western North Carolina\n***\\*\\*\\*Please 
 note: event listings are moving to the Shut Up & Write! website and this M
 eetup page will be closed in a few weeks. You will find our Tuesday night 
 events here: [https://www.shutupwrite.com/series/id2uT2JS7l00](https://www
 .shutupwrite.com/series/id2uT2JS7l00)\\*\\*\\****\n\n**Here's how it works
 .** Show up at or before 6:00. At 6:00\, we do some quick introductions. A
 fterward\, for a full 60 minutes (I'll set a timer!) we are heads-down wri
 ting. Writing what? A novel? You bet. Some poetry? Sure. Song lyrics? Your
  resume? That report you need to get to your boss before 8 AM or you'll *n
 eed* *to write* that resume? All of the above and more. Just shut up and w
 rite.\n\nSurrounding ourselves with other writers who are busy putting wor
 ds onto page (physical or virtual) keeps us all accountable and focused.\n
 \nWhen the timer goes off\, we'll check-in with each other and see how it 
 went. Afterward\, feel free to stay to chat and get to know your fellow wr
 iters\, or keep writing\, or take off.\n\nSocializing is optional and will
  happen after (or briefly before) the focused writing. This is a safe spac
 e to work on your craft. No one will read or critique your writing.\n\nFor
  more information about our events\, visit [https://shutupwrite.com](https
 ://shutupwrite.com).\n\n**What to Expect**\n\n* Roughly 15 minutes of intr
 oductions\n* 60 minutes of focused writing (somebody set a timer)!\n* Afte
 rward\, optional socializing\n\n**Being late is okay:** Just show up and g
 et settled\, then check in with the host after the session. (Look for the 
 person with the Shut Up & Write sign).\n\n**What Should I Bring?**\n\n* Wh
 atever you need to be able to write!\n* Earbuds/earplugs if you want to bl
 ock ambient noise.\n\n**Other Important Details:**\n\n***\\*\\*\\*Please n
 ote: event listings are moving to the Shut Up & Write! website and this Me
 etup page will be closed in a few weeks. You will find our Tuesday night e
 vents here: [https://www.shutupwrite.com/series/id2uT2JS7l00](https://www.
 shutupwrite.com/series/id2uT2JS7l00)\\*\\*\\****\n\nHOSTS: This is a multi
 -host event\, so most of the time there will be a host present. If we are 
 unlucky and no host can attend\, please find each other and self-organize.
  Pay attention to the event chat and comments to see who is available.\n\n
 WI-FI: Yes!\n\nPARKING: Street parking in metered spots is free after 6pm.
  Closest municipal garages ($2/hour) are Wall St. & Coxe Street/Sears Alle
 y.
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/shutupandwriteasheville/events/314426
 235/
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CREATED:20260422T221514Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260422T221514Z
CLASS:PUBLIC
END:VEVENT
