BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Ncarboretum": "https://www.ncarboretum.org/event/nature-journaling-3/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:ncarboretum
X-SOURCE:NC Arboretum
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260515T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260515T120000
DTSTAMP:20260501T231958
CREATED:20260330T161834Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260330T161834Z
UID:10017022-1778839200-1778846400@www.ncarboretum.org
SUMMARY:Nature Journaling
DESCRIPTION:Nature Journaling\nwith Andrew Dundas \nFriday\, May 15  |  10 – 12pm \nBRN – Elective  |  BREG – Elective \nREGISTER HERE \nNature journaling fosters a connection to the outdoors unique to each individual who pursues it. It can be a means to practice art or poetry\, a therapeutic moment of reflection\, or scientific exploration of the ecosystems around us. Join arboretum staff in a review of the principles of nature journaling\, exploration of other’s work\, and visits to multiple sites across the Arboretum with optional prompts and tips for journaling. Basic supplies will be provided\, such as notebooks and writing/drawing utensils\, but you are also welcome to bring your own.  \nThis program will take place outside and will follow easy trails and paved walkways. Dress for the weather and prepare to be outside for the entire program time.  \nAndrew Dundas is an Adult Education employee with a passion for history\, folklore\, writing\, and nature. He studied journalism and visual storytelling at the University of Chapel Hill before joining the Arboretum’s Youth Education Department and later the Adult Education Department.  \n\nMembers: Remember to enter your promo code upon checkout to receive your 10% member discount! Email adulteducation@ncarboretum.org with questions.\nSee a full listing of Adult Education Programs at the North Carolina Arboretum here! Questions? Check our FAQs.\nWe are committed to fostering a diverse\, supportive learning community. If the cost of a class is a barrier for you\, please complete this scholarship form and we will see what kind of assistance we can provide.\nFollow us on Facebook & Instagram!\nJoin our Adult Education Student Hub on Discord!\nInterested in supporting the NC Arboretum more directly? Donate to the ONE Fund here.\n\nSee all of our classes open for registration here!
URL:https://www.ncarboretum.org/event/nature-journaling-3/
CATEGORIES:Adult Education
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://www.ncarboretum.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/12/Adult-Ed-Course-Jpgs.jpg
END:VEVENT
