X-SOURCE-URLS:{"NC Arboretum": "https://www.ncarboretum.org/event/guided-trail-walk-5/2026-05-16/"}
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Ncarboretum": "https://www.ncarboretum.org/event/guided-trail-walk-6/2026-05-16/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:ncarboretum
X-SOURCE:NC Arboretum
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260516T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260516T120000
DTSTAMP:20260501T231958
CREATED:20260408T153754Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260408T153754Z
UID:10017158-1778925600-1778932800@www.ncarboretum.org
SUMMARY:Guided Trail Walk
DESCRIPTION:Hit the trails and learn more about The North Carolina Arboretum’s botanically diverse forest with a guided trail walk! April through October\, this free hiking program is led by trained volunteer guides who take small groups of participants along woodland trails and through a variety of forest types. Depending on the season and each guide’s area of expertise\, topics of discussion may include wildflowers\, plant and tree identification\, natural history and more. \nGuided trail walks are limited to 15 people\, including the guide\, and are not recommended for guests under 16 years of age. Groups depart from the Baker Visitor Center Lobby on Tuesdays at 1 p.m. and Saturdays at 10 a.m. and 1 p.m.. \nWalks last 1.5 – 2.5 hours\, are approximately one to two miles in length. As this program is held rain or shine\, all participants should dress appropriately for the weather. \nThere is no pre-registration; walks are first-come first served and sign up sheets are located in the Baker Visitors Center. \nWalks are FREE; however\, donations to The North Carolina Arboretum Society are appreciated. Regular parking fees apply. Arboretum Society Members always park free. \nKnow Before You Go\n\nGuided Trail Walks are not recommended for guests under 16 years of age.\nGuided Trail Walks are rain or shine and all participants should be dressed comfortably and for the weather.\nHikes cover 1-2 miles and last 1.5-2 hours.\nWell-behaved leashed pets are welcome to accompany their owners. In the rare case that a pet is disruptive or negatively impacts the experience\, the pet and its owner may be asked to excuse themselves from the guided walk.
URL:https://www.ncarboretum.org/event/guided-trail-walk-6/2026-05-16/
CATEGORIES:Guided Trail Walk
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://www.ncarboretum.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/Birders-on-Cove-Hardwood-Trail-GSMNP-TN-Apr-16-1-1.jpg
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Riverartsdistrict": "https://www.riverartsdistrict.com/event/soul-stitches-autobiographical-embroidery-with-guest-artist-elizabeth-garlington/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:riverartsdistrict
X-SOURCE:River Arts District
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260516T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260516T160000
DTSTAMP:20260501T232001
CREATED:20260413T120003Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260413T120003Z
UID:10035756-1778925600-1778947200@www.riverartsdistrict.com
SUMMARY:Soul Stitches: Autobiographical Embroidery with guest artist Elizabeth Garlington
DESCRIPTION:This two-day immersive workshop explores the intuitive process of embroidered fabric collage. \nWe will explore fiber art that explores themes of resilience and healing via the art of hand sewing and embroidered words on fabric as an added element to the collage process. \nOpen to all skill levels\, students will first learn foundational embroidery techniques by creating a “sampler” of running and back stitches\, including lettering. Students will learn to embroider text based on their own journal writings and important quotes. \nFavorite fabrics and/or vintage linen as base fabrics are encouraged as this element will bring an additional layer of meaning to our process/product. This introspective workshop invites personal exploration and collective connection. Inspired by story\, life experiences\, and playing with many colors of embroidery floss\, threads\, yarns\, and fabrics\, students will take inspiration from their daily life and written expression to create an original embroidered work of fabric collage art which could lead to a meditative daily art practice. \nThis class is a place to find your own unique making. \nStudents are encouraged to bring: any journal writings\, meaningful quotes\, written expressions\, as well as favorite fabrics and/or vintage linen as their base fabric–all bringing an additional layer of meaning to this art form. The purchase of a 6” and 10” embroidery hoop is suggested so that the embroidery process you begin in this workshop can be continued in your own time and space. \nThis is a beginner-friendly workshop and no experience is needed! Come as you are!
URL:https://www.riverartsdistrict.com/event/soul-stitches-autobiographical-embroidery-with-guest-artist-elizabeth-garlington/
LOCATION:ArtPlay Studio\, 53 Orange Street\, Asheville\, NC\, 28801
CATEGORIES:Classes
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/png:https://www.riverartsdistrict.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/03/Screenshot-2026-03-16-at-3.04.43-PM.png
ORGANIZER;CN="ArtPlay Studio":MAILTO:info@artplaystudio.com
GEO:35.5807036;-82.5639429
