BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Ashevilleart": "https://www.ashevilleart.org/event/exhibition-on-screen-raphael-revealed/2026-05-24/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:ashevilleart
X-SOURCE:Asheville Art Museum
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260524T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260524T160000
DTSTAMP:20260501T231944
CREATED:20251229T185536Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20251230T150756Z
UID:10005969-1779631200-1779638400@www.ashevilleart.org
SUMMARY:Exhibition on Screen | Raphael Revealed
DESCRIPTION:Marking the 500th anniversary of Raphael’s death\, the greatest exhibition ever held of his works took place in Rome. Exhibition on Screen was granted exclusive access to this once-in-a-lifetime show. With over two hundred masterpieces\, including paintings and drawings – over a hundred of which have been brought together for the first time – this major exhibition celebrates the life and work of Raffaello Sanzio da Urbino. \nWith unprecedented loans from the Louvre\, Uffizi\, National Gallery of Art\, the Prado Museum and more\, the exhibition and this film provide an unprecedented opportunity to see the breadth of Raphael’s skill\, creativity and ingenuity. Award-winning director Phil Grabsky provides a fresh look at this giant of the Renaissance\, and shows why he is considered one of the all-time greats. The film covers his life in Rome\, and includes unique footage of the ancient Rome that was such a powerful influence\, including rare footage of Nero’s Golden House that Raphael himself visited. \nMore than just a painter\, Raphael was one of the most extraordinary artists of the Renaissance but is often misunderstood or mythologised. On the basis of this extraordinary exhibition in Rome\, this film allows Raphael\, for the first time\, to be truly revealed. Directed by Phil Grabsky. \nPurchase Tickets
URL:https://www.ashevilleart.org/event/exhibition-on-screen-raphael-revealed/2026-05-24/
LOCATION:NC
CATEGORIES:Film
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://www.ashevilleart.org/wp-content/uploads/MV5BZDJjMzg2MDYtNjFmYS00ZWU0LTlhMDEtYzJlOGU5YmQwZDcwXkEyXkFqcGc@._V1_FMjpg_UX1000_.jpg
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Meetup Haywood County Walking Meetup Group": "https://www.meetup.com/haywood-county-walking-meetup-group/events/314137743/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:meetup_haywood_county_walking_meetup_group
X-SOURCE:Haywood County Walking Group
UID:event_314137743@meetup.com
SEQUENCE:1
DTSTAMP:20260502T031955Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260524T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260524T160000
SUMMARY:Holiday Weekend Sunday Walk at Little Champion Plant in Waynesvill
 e
DESCRIPTION:Haywood County Walking Meetup Group\nWhat better way to spend 
 the Sunday afternoon before Memorial Day than by walking with a meetup gro
 up?\n\nOld Timers call this property on Old Howell Mill Road near Old Ashe
 ville Highway "Little Champion" because the Canton Champion Paper Mill put
  in this plant to put wax on paper for making milk cartons. The Mill chang
 ed hands several times\, but the Old Timers kept calling it Little Champio
 n. (Note that Google Maps calls it Evergreen Packaging\, and the sign on t
 he building now says Suzano.)\n\nThe 3/4-mile walking track at Little Cham
 pion runs by Richland Creek with lots of creekside trees\, by fishing spot
 s\, and by a picnic area. There is a bathroom in the middle of the track. 
 We plan to do 4 clockwise laps. (Yes\, you are free to do fewer or even mo
 re!) That will make a total of 5 KM/3.1 miles.\n\nBe sure you enter the pr
 operty on the Old Asheville Highway (east) side of the plant (the side wit
 h the Suzano sign) on Ken Thompson Drive\, go to the rear of the building\
 , and then turning left\, go ***all the way to the far end of the back of 
 the parking lot\, down by the sign designating the Drop Lot***. It is in t
 hat corner of the parking lot where we will assemble. (If you go down the 
 stairs into the middle of the track\, you will be in the wrong place and w
 ill miss where the group is assembling.)\n\nDress appropriately for the we
 ather\; consider a hat and sunscreen. There is a little hill on each lap\,
  so some may want walking sticks. Bring plenty of water and a protein snac
 k. This is a paved track\, so tennis shoes will be fine. Dogs are welcome.
  Strollers will have no problem.
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/haywood-county-walking-meetup-group/e
 vents/314137743/
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CREATED:20260405T201740Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260405T201740Z
CLASS:PUBLIC
END:VEVENT
